    16	E-02 on this side: every signature is logged (request id, frame SHA-256, signature SHA-256) before its response is
    17	sent. A request delivered twice in one run gets the same signature again, not a second one. Across runs there is no
    18	memory: a request redelivered after its response was sent (a failed delete) is signed again, and the issuer records
    19	the second response as a duplicate. sign_by bounds how late that can happen."""
